A component is considered a practical runtime bottleneck if its latency exceeds 10% of total inference latency. If full PLM forward latency is unavailable, report relative bottleneck analysis using `agg_match_ratio` and total MeMR overhead.
Memory bottleneck should be discussed based on linear growth of task-related memory and available GPU memory.

